## Model card

- **Name:** MiniMax M3.1 Flash Preview
- **Short description:** Verified multimodal coding preview. This is not presumed to be Space Bunny or the existing M3 checkpoint.
- **Provider / access:** M Plan and MiniMax Code only at present. Documented Chat Completions at `https://api.minimax.io/v1/chat/completions`; an Anthropic-compatible interface also exists. [Model availability](https://platform.minimax.io/docs/guides/models-intro), [API](https://platform.minimax.io/docs/api-reference/text-chat-openai)
- **Release / knowledge:** Exact official launch date and knowledge cutoff not verified; independent evaluation recorded September 28, 2026.
- **IDs:** `MiniMax-M3.1-Flash-Preview`; no verified Zen Free ID.
- **Context window:** 1M tokens; maximum output unverified. [Official model table](https://platform.minimax.io/docs/guides/models-intro)
- **Modalities:** Text/image/video input, text output, tools; mandatory thinking with low/medium/high/xhigh/max effort, default max. JSON-schema enforcement unverified. [API specifications](https://platform.minimax.io/docs/api-reference/text-chat-openai)
- **Pricing (as of 2026-10-07):** Subscription access confirmed; exact per-million input/output/cache prices not verified. The [official price table](https://platform.minimax.io/docs/pricing/overview) lists M3 rates, which must not be transferred to M3.1. [M Plan documentation](https://platform.minimax.io/docs/m-plan/intro) confirms inclusion across its tiers, without enough usage/cost detail here to calculate comparable token economics. Privacy terms not independently evaluated.
- **Architecture:** Parameters, active size, topology and weight license unverified; no M3 architecture extrapolation.

### Raw benchmarks found

Agent / tool use:
- Terminal-Bench 2.1, Tau3/Tau2, GDPval-AA, Claw-Eval, Toolathon and MCP-Atlas: no verified public score found.

Reasoning / knowledge:
- GPQA Diamond, HLE, LCR/MLCR, CritPt, AA Intelligence Index and Omniscience: no verified public score found.
- ModelDial max-effort knowledge/reasoning: **75/100**, limited private task set.

Coding:
- ModelDial max effort: backend/testing **75/100**, frontend/interaction **57/100**; its own weighted overall **69.6/100**, rank **19/33**, evaluation time **54m 7s**, reference cost unavailable. Backend test dated September 28; snapshot October 5, 2026. [Evaluator's results](https://modeldial.com/en/models/MiniMax-M3.1-Flash-Preview?axis=overall&config=MiniMax-M3.1-Flash-Preview~max)
- SWE-bench, DeepSWE, LiveCodeBench, SciCode and Vibe Code Bench: no verified public score found.

Long context:
- No verified retrieval score found for the advertised 1M window.

Evidence limitations:
- ModelDial is a primary evaluator, not a vendor benchmark announcement. Its [methodology](https://modeldial.com/en/method) uses five backend questions, a frontend application exercise and twenty reasoning questions; the aggregate weights are 40/30/30. Its [datasets](https://modeldial.com/en/datasets) are private. This is useful narrow evidence but not equivalent to the project's agent/science/coding benchmark ladder.
- Neither private-suite scores nor M3's published results are substituted for missing M3.1 measurements.

### Normalized scores (1–100)

Self-excluded for insufficient calibrated evidence across the quality dimensions, particularly tool execution and broad reasoning. Some verified narrow benchmark results exist; this is not a zero-evidence or nonexistent-model verdict. Comparable token cost also remains unknown. No placeholder scores or Overall are assigned. Revisit when broader evaluations and pricing are published.

